      "bullets": [
        "OpenAI's affiliated super PAC is reportedly funding AI-generated news outlets to publish targeted political attacks against industry and regulatory critics.",
        "The strategy highlights how LLM-driven automated content pipelines are increasingly deployed for targeted political influence operations and astroturfing.",
        "AI practitioners face escalating reputational and regulatory risks as foundation model vendors leverage their own technology for covert lobbying."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Retries don't fix eventual consistency",
      "url": "https://var0.xyz/posts/retries-dont-fix-eventual-consistency.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/t0cn1z",
      "score": 2,
      "comments": 0,
      "author": "var0xyz",
      "published": "2026-08-03T08:36:37Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Immediate client retries hit stale cache windows or read replicas without enforcing read-after-write synchronization guarantees across distributed nodes.",
        "Mitigate read stale-ness using session tokens for read-your-own-writes consistency or switching critical database operations to strong consistency modes.",
        "Resolve write conflicts through optimistic concurrency control with monotonic version vectors or asynchronous outbox event processing instead of blocking retries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
