      "bullets": [
        "Firmware reverse-engineering of TP-Link TL-841N routers exposes hardcoded administrative credentials baked directly into the device filesystem.",
        "Factory resets fail to clear these embedded credentials, leaving SOHO devices permanently compromised once exposed to local or WAN attacks.",
        "Root access achieved via serial interfaces or firmware extraction underscores risks of legacy consumer hardware lacking secure boot mechanisms."
      ]
